+From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: BCM5301X: add port 5 back for the flow accelerator
+
+Patch 376 makes port 8 (gmac2) the only CPU port and disables port 5
+(gmac0). Behind the flow accelerator in front of port 8, b53 needs
+port 5 as a second CPU port: it redirects the frames that the
+accelerator must not handle there (TTL or hop limit 1, TCP FIN and
+RST). With both CPU ports, b53 chooses the accelerator's prepended
+tag on a switch that has the accelerator, and the regular tag on one
+that has not, so the change is safe on every Northstar board. User
+ports keep port 8 as their CPU port.
+
+Enable port 5 again, with a fixed link, on the boards where 376 or the
+board itself disabled it. Not on the boards where port 5 has another
+use (RT-AC87U, RT-AC88U) or where gmac0 is off (Meraki MR26, MR32), and
+not on the boards that keep port 5 as their only CPU port. The ASUS
+RT-N18U gets it from 379.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
